# Start a new blueprint change

Run:

```sh
blueprint new "<intent>" --json
```

The JSON contains the change `id`, routed `tier`, and the path to `.blueprint/changes/<id>/change.md`.
Open that change.md: fill the EARS Delta (every requirement needs a machine-settleable `verify` method)
and the Tasks checklist before writing any code. The loop contract in the TOML frontmatter is binding.
